(12820, 0, 'cstreeview', 1, '0.0.1', 915, 26, 'Generic tree view', 'FE plugin to let the reader view a tree of related data (table rows)', 3, 0, 3, 1163288714, 'a:0:{}', 'Christian Stdemann', 'typo3@christian-stuedemann.de', 'stuedemann', '3540500c75fefe8caebfc61f5f7db0dd', 'This is the very first version of cstreeview. The documentation is not completed, but shows the most recent issues. Please dont hesitate to ask me about details. I will update the implementation and documentation continuously.', '', 1, 0, 0),
(12821, 0, 'cstreeview', 1, '0.0.2', 915, 194, 'Generic tree view', 'FE plugin to let the reader view a tree of related data (table rows)', 0, 0, 3, 1163289629, 'a:0:{}', 'Christian Stdemann', 'typo3@christian-stuedemann.de', 'stuedemann', 'f33331f3c6e1b2168af1c3085a9f1deb', 'First tests were successful. Changing from "experimental" to "alpha".', '', 2, 0, 0),
(12822, 0, 'cstreeview', 1, '0.0.3', 915, 229, 'Generic tree view', 'FE plugin to let the reader view a tree of related data (table rows)', 0, 0, 3, 1163455587, 'a:0:{}', 'Christian Stdemann', 'typo3@christian-stuedemann.de', 'stuedemann', '529d13d286e12aca6354da4acd2e4c9d', 'Bugfix. The bug was: If compareToParentField was defined and returned no results, a default uid-pid-relation was executed afterwards by mistake. Correct behavior is now: If compareToParent Field is defined and returns no results, the result ("nothing") is', '', 3, 0, 0),
(12823, 0, 'cstreeview', 1, '0.0.4', 915, 191, 'Generic tree view', 'FE plugin to let the reader view a tree of related data (table rows)', 0, 0, 3, 1167178332, 'a:0:{}', 'Christian Stdemann', 'typo3@christian-stuedemann.de', 'stuedemann', '7ac630bbf04abfc5fac9a22f6251f3ee', 'Fixed a bug for PHP5.x concerning "static leaves". They did not work because of a recursion. Extended the documentation. Added the KEY marker.', '', 4, 0, 0),
(12824, 0, 'cstreeview', 1, '0.0.5', 915, 275, 'Generic FE treeview', 'FE plugin to display DB-content in a hierarchical treeview. Appearance of the treeview-structure, appearance of the data and relationship between the hierarchies can be configured in wide ranges.', 0, 0, 3, 1167501678, 'a:0:{}', 'Christian Stuedemann', 'typo3@christian-stuedemann.de', 'stuedemann', '26100c0f243f482d3a21cce9b26a374f', 'Bugfix: Additional (sensless & incorrect) SQL statements were executed. Thanks to Janno S. from NL for reporting this bug. - Added the LEVEL marker. - Added the TS parameter defaultStatus. Note: Stored treestatus for FE users will be reset!', '', 5, 1, 0),
